 "mandate_proposal.notes[0]": "the contribution of 12,000 a year is the household's stated yearly saving, read as going wholly to this goal in twelve monthly steps; savings shared with other goals would make the required return higher than shown",
 "mandate_proposal.notes[1]": "the goal's amount 1,500,000 is in today's francs (the request does not say; decision 7: today by default) and is inflated to its date at 1.00% a year (CHF, price level 1.1523): 1,728,505.78 in francs of the target date",
 "mandate_proposal.notes[2]": "the contribution is fixed in francs (the request does not say; decision 9: fixed by default), so its purchasing power falls by 1.00% a year",
 "mandate_proposal.notes[3]": "the goal is already funded at a zero return: the mandate is capital preservation",
 "mandate_proposal.notes[4]": "the risk profile also interpolates asset-class bounds {'Cash': {'lower': 0.0, 'upper': 0.22080096696212737}, 'Equity': {'lower': 0.0, 'upper': 0.6381692183722804}}; asset class is a policy dimension, so they are a suggestion for the curator and not a derived bound",
 "mandate_proposal.notes[5]": "funded at a zero nominal return, which is -0.99% a year in real terms; the real required return is at most that",
